model {
  extend basalt.frameworkRelease {
    metadata {
      constraint "Every host build embeds all canonical and qualified production framework identities plus its checked producer before bundling. Only the trusted release records a candidate-bound producer qualification with exact runtime.json and framework.json hashes in the existing production deployment ledger before activation. Production rereads both files and verifies their identical runtime bytes, the exact producer, complete history and generated registry before recording. Failed or unknown activation never removes qualification; later hosts retain all earlier qualified identities. Approved pre-enrollment releases are canonical qualifications bound to pinned rebuild evidence and never claim a serving-byte match. A freshly prepared host admits canonical framework bytes without producer enrollment; each newly committed identity must match the exact server, browser and runtime bytes from its reviewed Linux source build. Previously canonical publication tuples remain byte-identical when a later browser publication is added under the same protocol. Canonical build inputs remain separate from the generated runtime registry so Worker bundles embed history once. Compact generated storage decodes to the identical ordered publication tuples and hashes before admission. Offline source verification reproduces preparation replacement semantics and accepts generated registry data only against the checked candidate, producer, canonical identities and both publication hashes. App builds cannot enroll identities, and runtime admission remains offline and exact."
    }
  }
}
